# Patent Description

## Detailed Description of the Invention

A display device comprising:

a base substrate defining a plurality of recesses formed therein;

a reflective layer disposed within each of said recesses, said reflective layer being configured to reflect incident light;

a light-transmissive filler material disposed within each of said recesses and overlying said reflective layer;

a first transparent electrode and a second transparent electrode arranged in opposing relation;

an organic light-emitting layer disposed between and in contact with said first transparent electrode and said second transparent electrode, said organic light-emitting layer being configured to emit light upon application of an electrical potential across said first and second transparent electrodes; and

a plurality of thin-film transistors electrically coupled to said first and second transparent electrodes, said thin-film transistors being configured to selectively drive respective pixels of the display device;

wherein said reflective layer is electrically conductive and is further configured to function as an electrical contact for the corresponding pixel, whereby said reflective layer serves both a light-reflecting function and an electrical-conducting function.

---

**Note:** I have rendered your description into conventional patent claim/specification language. You may wish to consider the following refinements:

- **Antecedent basis:** Ensure each element is first introduced with "a"/"an" and thereafter referenced with "said" or "the."
- **Clarify the electrode-reflector relationship:** The phrase "mirror layer doubling as the electrical contact" would benefit from specifying whether the reflective layer *replaces* one of the transparent electrodes or supplements it.
- **Dependent claims:** Consider drafting dependent claims covering specific materials (e.g., metallic reflective layers), recess geometries, and filler compositions to broaden protection.
